# What `docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile .` may not see. The Dockerfile
# copies only the API, the three workspace packages it runs and the workspace
# manifests, so everything here is either a secret, a build output, another
# tool's state, or bulk the image has no use for. The web app is left out
# whole but for its manifest, which the frozen-lockfile check reads.
.git
.github
.claude
**/node_modules
.env
.env.*
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
docs
e2e
supabase
test-results
playwright-report
.playwright-cli
.playwright-mcp
.superpowers
.windsurf
**/*.md
apps/web/**
!apps/web/package.json
# The DAWA snapshot, reference data for an import that has not been written.
packages/db/reference
# Tests, which run in CI and have no reader in the image.
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
# The recipe itself: BuildKit reads it beside the context, not from it.
apps/api/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
